# MiniMax-M3 fp8-static + CHUNKED-PREFILL — run the GLM-5.2 Tier-0 prefill-ramp lever on M3 (GQA).
# ===================================================================================================
# MINIMAL one-lever diff from the coherent champion minimax-m3-fp8-static.env:
#   VLLM_ARGS  += --enable-chunked-prefill --max-num-batched-tokens 4096   (decode-priority scheduling)
#   MODEL_ENV  += HPU_STEP_TIMER=1 HPU_STEP_TIMER_N=50                      (decode step timing, telemetry)
# EVERYTHING ELSE identical to fp8-static -> clean A/B (the only deltas are the chunked-prefill flag,
# its 4096 token budget, and the step timer which is on the env-knob-guard EXCLUDE list = no cache wipe).
#
# WHY on M3: M3 is GQA, KV ~120 KB/tok (fp8-KV halves to ~60), so it is KV-bound and its real-world
# aggregate is dragged by the SAME prefill ramp (cold-JIT tax + many-prompt prefill wave) that costs
# GLM-5.2 its c128 regression. prefill_prime.sh (warm recipe cache) + chunked-prefill (decode flows
# during the prefill wave) attack that ramp on the END-TO-END tokps.py metric.
#
# KV/OOM NOTE: the KV pool is sized by --gpu-memory-utilization (fills HBM after weights), NOT by
# --max-num-seqs, so c128 will not OOM at load — it simply ADMITS fewer than 128 seqs if the pool is
# full (like the GLM int4 collapse). At 4096 ctx M3 admits ~all at c<=64; c128 may shed streams.
# Test c1/32/64 (safe) + attempt c128 (report admitted count). If a card OOMs at LOAD, drop
# --max-model-len to 2048 or --max-num-seqs to 64 (the static env's own fallback note).
#
# COHERENCE GATE: route-b must engage ("LIVE: routed fp8 experts via UNFUSED swigluoai") and greedy
# text must be coherent (not silu salad). chunked-prefill is a scheduler lever, orthogonal to the
# route-b MoE path + GQA attention (verified read-only against the runner + m3 plugin).
# ===================================================================================================
MODEL_PATH=MiniMax-M3-fp8-experts-AutoRound
SERVED_NAME=minimax-m3
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
EXTRA_MOUNTS="-v $HOME/AI/minimax-m3/vllm:/opt/m3-vllm -v $HOME/AI/minimax-m3:/opt/m3-root -v $HOME/AI/hpu-moe-ext/hpu_moe_ext/fused_monolithic_moe_fp8.py:/opt/hpu-moe-ext/hpu_moe_ext/fused_monolithic_moe_fp8.py -v $HOME/AI/hpu-moe-ext/tpc_kernel/opbackend/build/libmoe_fused_monolithic_fp8_lazy.so:/opt/hpu-moe-ext/tpc_kernel/opbackend/build/libmoe_fused_monolithic_fp8_lazy.so -v $HOME/AI/vllm-gaudi-patch/worker/hpu_model_runner.py:/opt/vllm-gaudi/vllm_gaudi/v1/worker/hpu_model_runner.py"
MODEL_ENV="-e M3_VLLM_DIR=/opt/m3-vllm -e M3_ROOT_DIR=/opt/m3-root -e M3_FP8_STATIC=1 -e M3_SWIGLUOAI=1 -e M3_FP8_SWIGLU_ROUTE=b -e VLLM_HPU_FORCE_CHANNEL_FP8=true -e VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=fork -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=3600 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 -e VLLM_HPU_LOG_STEP_CPU_FALLBACKS=true -e HPU_STEP_TIMER=1 -e HPU_STEP_TIMER_N=50"
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization compressed-tensors --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc --tensor-parallel-size 8 --enable-expert-parallel --block-size 128 --max-num-seqs 128 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --max-model-len 4096 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code --enable-chunked-prefill --max-num-batched-tokens 4096"
